Lab 1: Introduction to Red Hat Satellite 6
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the core components and architecture of Red Hat Satellite 6
Successfully install and configure Red Hat Satellite 6 on a Linux system
Identify and explain the roles of key Satellite components: Capsule, Smart Proxy, Pulp, Foreman, and Katello
Register Red Hat Satellite to Red Hat Subscription Management (RHSM)
Navigate the Satellite web interface and understand basic functionality
Demonstrate understanding of Satellite's role in enterprise system management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic knowledge of Linux system administration
Understanding of package management concepts (RPM, YUM/DNF)
Familiarity with command-line interface operations
Basic networking concepts (DNS, DHCP, HTTP/HTTPS)
Understanding of subscription management concepts
Access to Red Hat Developer account (free registration available)
Lab Environment
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click Start Lab to access your environment - no need to build your own virtual machine or configure hardware.

Your lab environment includes:

Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8 or 9 server with minimum 20GB RAM and 300GB storage
Internet connectivity for package downloads and registration
